## Key Technical Decisions

- **KTD-1 — Unresolved SPH-DEM coupling, not resolved collision.** Water↔grain interaction is a body force from a locally-averaged porosity field + drag closure (Robinson 2013), **not** sphere-sphere non-penetration (which causes porous locking, spurious collision-pressure, bed dilation). User-specified and literature-standard.
- **KTD-2 — Keep `α_s` as the volume channel, but back it with an explicit retention floor; remove exclusion only after drag lands.** `α_s` density modulation alone is **not** a hard barrier (a sparse/under-neighbored water particle can advect through, pool below, or ghost in high-α_s zones — Codex r1.1). So: (a) enforce a **minimum-porosity floor** in the water density target and a **residual porous resistance** (a weak `∇α_s`-driven volumetric penalty / a strong near-saturation drag limit — *not* sphere exclusion) so water is hydraulically retained; (b) **land the Darcy drag first** (U3) and remove exclusion **under** that drag (U2), gated by a "no free-fall through a static bed" test (Codex r1.2). Removal stays the goal; retention is the explicit safety net.
- **KTD-3 — Darcy drag: viscous-only, exponential, PAIR-SYMMETRIC, AGGREGATE-NORMALIZED, RESOLUTION-NORMALIZED.** Per-grain Darcy `β = 150·μ·(1−ε)²/(ε³·d²)` (Kozeny–Carman structure, already `porosity_drag_factor ∝ d⁻²`). Drop the Ergun inertial term (Darcian). To conserve momentum under *asymmetric per-particle porosity* (Codex r1.3): form a **symmetric pair coefficient** `β_ij` from stored per-particle coefficients (deterministic harmonic combiner), one pair impulse `J_ij = m_eff_pair·(1 − e^(−Δt/τ_ij))·(u_j − u_i)`, applied `+J/m_i` and `−J/m_j` in the two mirrored gathers off `vel_frozen`. To avoid over-damping when summed over many neighbors (Codex r1.4): apply the exponential to the **aggregate** local drag (`β_i = Σ_j β_ij W_ij V_j`), distributing by normalized weights — *not* `1−e^{−dt/τ}` summed per pair. **Resolution-normalize** so the total drag force on a grain is invariant as water is refined (Codex r1.11) — done here, before U5. The exponential integrator is unconditionally stable (the current β-blend is its weak first-order approximation; the bug is the tiny rate).
- **KTD-4 — Mobilization is a separate, explicit criterion from stability (Codex r1.5).** Viscous drag damps; bed *rearrangement* requires the pour-zone drag impulse over a frame to **exceed** the surface grains' static-yield + contact + rolling resistance, while bulk-bed impulse stays **below** the fluidization threshold. This inequality is a calibration target and a gate, not an emergent hope.
- **KTD-5 — Wide coupling kernel `h_c`, water PBF keeps its own radius.** Compute `α_s`/drag porosity over `h_c ≈ 2–3× grain_diameter` for a smooth field; set `cell_size = max(h_c, grain_diameter, h)`, but the **water PBF density solve still distance-culls to its own `h`** (Codex r1.6) — the larger cell only widens the candidate list. Clamp `ε ∈ [0.35, 0.999]`. Instrument avg/max neighbor counts per pass (the wider gather can spike PBF/drag/sort cost).
- **KTD-6 — Reduced units; calibrate by BANDED multi-observable inequalities (Codex r1.8).** No SI system is wired (`KEEP.md §2`). Calibrate the one free drag scale against *several* bands simultaneously: coarse/fine drawdown ratio, bounded pour-zone displacement, a bulk-displacement ceiling, water-retention height, and zero long-run momentum/volume drift — one observable is under-determined. Real-unit conversion is deferred.
- **KTD-7 — Buoyancy separate AND not double-counted with drag (Codex r1.10).** Buoyancy stays `−V·∇P` over the PBF `λ` field (density-aware `grain_buoyancy_factor`). Because that pressure gradient already arises from the α_s-modified PBF constraint, ensure drag forces grains only from **relative velocity**, never re-applying the pressure-gradient term. Gate: a hydrostatic saturated bed at rest has zero net grain acceleration beyond buoyancy balance; a flowing bed receives drag from relative velocity only.
- **KTD-8 — `coupling_scale` lane allocation is explicit; 8-buffer budget held (Codex r1.9).** Precompute into the existing `coupling_scale: vec2<f32>`: `x = aggregate inverse-stopping-time (or β_i)`, `y = normalization (Σ W_ij V_j) or local ε`. Confirm **no pass needs `α_s`, `ε`, and `β` simultaneously** — derive ε from α_s at point of use. Add no bindings to the already-8/8 drag passes; never bit-pack two physical quantities into one lane.
- **KTD-9 — Normalized, decaying wake criterion (Codex r1.7).** Replace the raw `fluid_impulse > wake_threshold` (which scales with dt/subiters/neighbor count) with a **dimensionless** gate (drag impulse relative to grain submerged weight, or local relative-flow speed sustained over a minimum duration) and an explicit `fluid_impulse` decay/reset so saturated tails don't creep.
- **KTD-10 — Water finer than grains is realism, sequenced last with drag already resolution-normalized.** `R_w < R_s` improves the look + fluid detail but stresses CFL/kernel normalization (XSPH eruption lesson). Because KTD-3 resolution-normalizes drag, refinement won't change bed forcing; still run the spacing-invariance gate. Keep the count modest; defer the 200k push.

